 "notModeled": [
  "analog input and reference (REFIN/REFM; REFOUT never driven): every conversion returns the 0 V code 0000h (twos complement, -VREF to +VREF)",
  "conversion start: a CONVST falling edge starts a conversion only while CS is low (tsu1; CS must be low when CONVST falls); the model starts one at every CONVST falling edge; CS falling starts the acquisition period, which is not modeled",
  "conversion abort (a second CONVST falling edge with CS low, or a CS falling edge, within tsu(AB) of the start) is not modeled",
  "read latency: RD with CS low puts the previous conversion result on the bus on the part; the model's result is the constant 0 V code",
  "quiet-zone timing around the CONVST falling edge; BUSY delays tpd1/tpd2",
  "BYTE: the read pattern follows the BYTE level at the start of each read (BYTE high: D7-D0 on DB15-DB8, all ones on DB7-DB0); BYTE changes while RD stays low take effect at the next read in the model",
  "RESET low aborts the conversion and clears the output latches to zeros (the 0 V code is already zero); the first sampling period 20 ns after RESET rises is not modeled",
  "pin table order kept for pins 1-2 (REFIN 1, REFOUT 2)"
 ],
 "variants": "ADS8406IB only in the skeleton (both orderables are IB grade); the ADS8405 is the unipolar (straight binary) version in a separate datasheet",
